<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/main.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/homePage.css">
    <title>Document</title>
</head>
<body>
    <header><% if (user) { %>
            <%- include('../partials/header-logged-in.ejs'); %>
          <% } else if (!user) { %>
            <%- include('../partials/header-not-logged-in.ejs'); %>
          <% } else { %>
            <%- console.log("su'in else") %>
          <% } %>
    </header>

    <%- console.log('gyatuser : ', user) %>
    <main>
        <h1>Library Store Tool: a way to digitally store your home library in an online account so you can view and share your books with others</h1>

        <section>
    
            <p>
                If you really love books, and you have physical books whose details you want to record online, this site is for you
            </p>

            <p>Here's how to create your first collection and add a book to it:</p>

                <ul>
                <li>Start by clicking the Register button to set up an account </li> 

                <li>Then click the Login button to sign in </li>

                <li>Click the Your Collections button, then create a new collection using the ‘Make a new collection’ tool (e.g. Bedroom Books) </li>

                <li>Click the name of your new collection, and add books to it by putting the ISBN into the box on the right </li>

                </ul>
            
            <p>
                You can also search for the details of any book, by clicking on the Find a Book button and entering an ISBN.
            </p>

            <section id="whatIsAnISBNdiv">
                <img src="/images/CoverWithISBN.jpg" alt="" id="coverWithISBNimg">

                <div id="textDiv">
                    <h2>What is an ISBN?</h2>
                    <p> An ISBN is a 10 or 13 digit number which can uniquely identify any book<br>
                        Most of the time, you can turn over a book to find its ISBN near the barcode (see photo)<br>
                        You can also find a book's ISBN on the page at the front of the book with publication information
                    </p>
                </div>

            </section>

        </section>
    </main>


    
</body>
</html>